IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `snap-core`

-- Food and Nutrition Act of 2008 (7 U.S.C. ch. 51), section 2020 (Administration), subsections (a) to (d).
-- LAYER 1 (the law, objectively): written from the text alone, from no one's point of view.
-- The text is the converter's plain-text rendering (usc07-ch51.txt), not the official text.
-- Every rule below answers MAYBE BOOLEAN where the text decides something: JUST TRUE (the text says yes),
-- JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words) or NOTHING (the text does not say). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Lines are cited as `-- src:N | text` (copied from the raw file by a script) and `@ref ... (src:N-M)`.

-- inert: 1425 | reason 1 | the section heading
-- inert: 1426 | reason 1 | the subsection heading "State responsibility"

§ `s 2020(a) State responsibility`

-- The two shapes of administration the text names in (a)(2); the third constructor is the "not covered" value.
DECLARE `s 2020(a)(2) basis of operation` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(a)(2) State-administered`
    `s 2020(a)(2) county-administered`
    `s 2020(a)(2) administered on some other basis`

-- The four kinds of change the standards of (a)(4)(A) must reach, and a constructor for any other.
DECLARE `s 2020(a)(4)(A) kind of change in operations` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(a)(4)(A)(i) many low-income households live far from an office performing the major functions of subsection (e)`
    `s 2020(a)(4)(A)(ii) automated systems replace personnel described in subsection (e)(6)(B)`
    `s 2020(a)(4)(A)(iii) it is harder to report information under subsection (e) or section 2015(c)`
    `s 2020(a)(4)(A)(iv) the burdens grow disproportionately on a type of household in subsection (e)(2)(A)`
    `s 2020(a)(4)(A) any other change`

-- src:1428 | The State agency of each participating State shall have responsibility for certifying applicant households and issuing EBT cards.
-- jural: an applicant household | the State agency | claim and duty (inferred: the text names the State agency and the object of its duty, not who may enforce it)
@ref s 2020(a)(1) (src:1428)
GIVEN `the State participates in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
`s 2020(a)(1) the party responsible for certifying applicant households and issuing EBT cards` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State participates in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN JUST `the State agency`
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The State agency of each participating State"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1430 | The responsibility of the agency of the State government shall not be affected by whether the program is operated on a State-administered or county-administered basis, as provided under section 2012(s)(1) of this title.
-- jural: the State agency | none named | immunity: its responsibility is not affected by the mode of operation
@ref s 2020(a)(2) (src:1430)
GIVEN `the basis on which the program is operated` IS A `s 2020(a)(2) basis of operation`
      `s 2012(s) the body is a State agency` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(a)(2) the responsibility of the State agency is affected by the basis of operation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2012(s) the body is a State agency`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is a State agency is section 2012(s)'s answer and was not supplied
    WHEN JUST isAgency THEN
        BRANCH
            IF isAgency AND `the basis on which the program is operated` EQUALS `s 2020(a)(2) State-administered`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be affected by whether the program is operated on a State-administered or county-administered basis"
            IF isAgency AND `the basis on which the program is operated` EQUALS `s 2020(a)(2) county-administered`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be affected by whether the program is operated on a State-administered or county-administered basis"
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text names only the State-administered and the county-administered bases
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1433 | Each State agency shall keep such records as may be necessary to determine whether the program is being conducted in compliance with this chapter (including regulations issued under this chapter).
-- jural: the Secretary | each State agency | claim and duty (inferred: the records exist so that the Secretary can determine compliance)
@ref s 2020(a)(3)(A) (src:1433)
GIVEN `the record is necessary to determine whether the program is being conducted in compliance with this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(a)(3)(A) the State agency must keep the record` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the record is necessary to determine whether the program is being conducted in compliance with this chapter` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such records as may be necessary to determine whether the program is being conducted in compliance"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1435 | All records, and the entire information systems in which records are contained, that are covered in subparagraph (A) shall—
-- src:1436 | (i) be made available for inspection and audit by the Secretary, subject to data and security protocols agreed to by the State agency and Secretary;
-- src:1438 | (iii) be preserved for such period of not less than 3 years as may be specified in regulations.
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agency | claim and duty: records open to inspection and audit, subject to agreed protocols
@ref s 2020(a)(3)(B)(i) (src:1435-1438)
GIVEN `the request to inspect or audit is made by the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency and the Secretary have agreed data and security protocols` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(a)(3)(B)(i) the records and information systems must be made available for inspection and audit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the request to inspect or audit is made by the Secretary` AND `the State agency and the Secretary have agreed data and security protocols` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "be made available for inspection and audit by the Secretary, subject to data and security protocols agreed to by the State agency and Secretary"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1437 | (ii) subject to subsection (e)(8), be available for review in any action filed by a household to enforce any provision of this chapter (including regulations issued under this chapter); and
-- jural: a household | the State agency | claim and duty: the records are open to review in the household's own enforcement action, subject to (e)(8)
@ref s 2020(a)(3)(B)(ii) (src:1437)
GIVEN `the action is filed by a household to enforce a provision of this chapter or of its regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (e)(8) bars review of the record` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(a)(3)(B)(ii) the records must be available for review in the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the action is filed by a household to enforce a provision of this chapter or of its regulations` AND (NOT `subsection (e)(8) bars review of the record`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to subsection (e)(8), be available for review in any action filed by a household"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1438 | (iii) be preserved for such period of not less than 3 years as may be specified in regulations.
@ref s 2020(a)(3)(B)(iii) (src:1438)
GIVEN `the years for which the records are preserved` IS A NUMBER
      `the minimum number of years specified in regulations` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(a)(3)(B)(iii) the records are preserved for long enough` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the years for which the records are preserved` LESS THAN 3
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for such period of not less than 3 years"
        IF `the years for which the records are preserved` AT LEAST 3 AND `the minimum number of years specified in regulations` EQUALS NOTHING
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "as may be specified in regulations"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the minimum number of years specified in regulations`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for such period of not less than 3 years as may be specified in regulations" (the specified number is a supplied input)
            WHEN JUST spec THEN JUST (`the years for which the records are preserved` AT LEAST spec)

-- src:1441 | The Secretary shall develop standards for identifying major changes in the operations of a State agency, including—
-- src:1442 | (i) large or substantially-increased numbers of low-income households that do not live in reasonable proximity to an office performing the major functions described in subsection (e);
-- src:1443 | (ii) substantial increases in reliance on automated systems for the performance of responsibilities previously performed by personnel described in subsection (e)(6)(B);
-- src:1444 | (iii) changes that potentially increase the difficulty of reporting information under subsection (e) or section 2015(c) of this title; and
-- src:1445 | (iv) changes that may disproportionately increase the burdens on any of the types of households described in subsection (e)(2)(A).
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agencies | power and liability: the Secretary sets standards by which a change in operations is judged major
@ref s 2020(a)(4)(A) (src:1441-1445)
GIVEN `the change` IS A `s 2020(a)(4)(A) kind of change in operations`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(a)(4)(A) the Secretary's standards for identifying major changes must reach the change` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the change`
    WHEN `s 2020(a)(4)(A) any other change` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "standards for identifying major changes in the operations of a State agency, including"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1447 | If a State agency implements a major change in operations, the State agency shall—
-- src:1448 | (i) notify the Secretary; and
-- src:1449 | (ii) collect such information as the Secretary shall require to identify and correct any adverse effects on program integrity or access, including access by any of the types of households described in subsection (e)(2)(A).
-- jural: the Secretary | the State agency | claim and duty: notice of a major change, and information to correct adverse effects
@ref s 2020(a)(4)(B) (src:1447-1449)
GIVEN `the State agency implements a major change in operations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(a)(4)(B) the State agency must notify the Secretary and collect the required information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency implements a major change in operations` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a State agency implements a major change in operations, the State agency shall"

§ `s 2020(b) Correction of improper denials and underissuances`

-- src:1451 | When a State agency learns, through its own reviews under section 2025 of this title or other reviews, or through other sources, that it has improperly denied, terminated, or underissued benefits to an eligible household, the State agency shall promptly restore any improperly denied benefits to the extent required by subsection (e)(11) and section 2023(b) of this title, and shall take other steps to prevent a recurrence of such errors where such error was caused by the application of State agency practices, rules or procedures inconsistent with the requirements of this chapter or with regulations or policies of the Secretary issued under the authority of this chapter.
-- jural: an eligible household | the State agency | claim and duty: prompt restoration of improperly denied benefits, to the extent (e)(11) and s 2023(b) require
@ref s 2020(b) (src:1451)
GIVEN `the State agency has learned that it improperly denied benefits to an eligible household` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(b) the State agency must promptly restore the improperly denied benefits` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has learned that it improperly denied benefits to an eligible household` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "When a State agency learns, through its own reviews under section 2025 of this title or other reviews, or through other sources"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1451 | When a State agency learns, through its own reviews under section 2025 of this title or other reviews, or through other sources, that it has improperly denied, terminated, or underissued benefits to an eligible household, the State agency shall promptly restore any improperly denied benefits to the extent required by subsection (e)(11) and section 2023(b) of this title, and shall take other steps to prevent a recurrence of such errors where such error was caused by the application of State agency practices, rules or procedures inconsistent with the requirements of this chapter or with regulations or policies of the Secretary issued under the authority of this chapter.
@ref s 2020(b) (src:1451)
GIVEN `the State agency has learned that it improperly denied, terminated or underissued benefits to an eligible household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the error was caused by State agency practices, rules or procedures inconsistent with this chapter or with the regulations or policies of the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(b) the State agency must take other steps to prevent a recurrence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has learned that it improperly denied, terminated or underissued benefits to an eligible household`
            AND `the error was caused by State agency practices, rules or procedures inconsistent with this chapter or with the regulations or policies of the Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where such error was caused by the application of State agency practices, rules or procedures inconsistent with the requirements of this chapter"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `s 2020(c) Civil rights compliance`

DECLARE `s 2020(c)(1) ground of discrimination` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(c)(1) race`
    `s 2020(c)(1) sex`
    `s 2020(c)(1) religious creed`
    `s 2020(c)(1) national origin`
    `s 2020(c)(1) political affiliation`
    `s 2020(c)(1) some other ground`

-- src:1454 | In the certification of applicant households for the supplemental nutrition assistance program, there shall be no discrimination by reason of race, sex, religious creed, national origin, or political affiliation.
-- jural: an applicant household | the State agency | immunity: certification must not turn on a named ground (disability of the agency to discriminate)
@ref s 2020(c)(1) (src:1454)
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `s 2020(c)(1) ground of discrimination`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(c)(1) the certification of applicant households may discriminate by reason of the ground` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `s 2020(c)(1) some other ground` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the five named grounds only; the text is silent on any other ground (subsection (c)(2) points to other laws outside the text)
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there shall be no discrimination by reason of race, sex, religious creed, national origin, or political affiliation"

DECLARE `s 2020(c)(2) law whose rights the administration must respect` IS ONE OF
    `s 2020(c)(2)(A) the Age Discrimination Act of 1975`
    `s 2020(c)(2)(B) section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973`
    `s 2020(c)(2)(C) the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990`
    `s 2020(c)(2)(D) title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964`
    `s 2020(c)(2) some other law`

-- src:1456 | The administration of the program by a State agency shall be consistent with the rights of households under the following laws (including implementing regulations):
-- src:1457 | (A) The Age Discrimination Act of 1975 (42 U.S.C. 6101 et seq.).
-- src:1458 | (B) Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 (29 U.S.C. 794).
-- src:1459 | (C) The Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990 (42 U.S.C. 12101 et seq.).
-- src:1460 | (D) Title VI of the Civil Rights Act of 1964 (42 U.S.C. 2000d et seq.).
-- jural: a household | the State agency | claim and duty: administration consistent with the household's rights under the four laws (including implementing regulations)
@ref s 2020(c)(2) (src:1456-1460)
GIVEN `the law` IS A `s 2020(c)(2) law whose rights the administration must respect`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(c)(2) the administration of the program must be consistent with the household's rights under the law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the law`
    WHEN `s 2020(c)(2) some other law` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "the following laws (including implementing regulations)" is a list without "only"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `s 2020(d) Plan of operation by State agency; approval by Secretary; Indians`

-- src:1462 | The State agency (as defined in section 2012(s)(1) of this title) of each State desiring to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program shall submit for approval a plan of operation specifying the manner in which such program will be conducted within the State in every political subdivision. …
-- jural: the Secretary | each State agency of a State desiring to participate | claim and duty: a plan of operation is submitted for approval
@ref s 2020(d) (src:1462)
GIVEN `s 2012(s) the body is a State agency` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the State desires to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(d) the State agency must submit a plan of operation for approval` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 2012(s) the body is a State agency`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body is a State agency is section 2012(s)'s answer and was not supplied
    WHEN JUST isAgency THEN
        BRANCH
            IF isAgency AND `the State desires to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The State agency ... of each State desiring to participate"
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1462 | The Secretary may not, as a part of the approval process for a plan of operation, require a State to submit for prior approval by the Secretary the State agency instructions to staff, interpretations of existing policy, State agency methods of administration, forms used by the State agency, or any materials, documents, memoranda, bulletins, or other matter, unless the State determines that the materials, documents, memoranda, bulletins, or other matter alter or amend the State plan of operation or conflict with the rights and levels of benefits to which a household is entitled. …
-- jural: the State | the Secretary | immunity and disability: the Secretary may not demand prior approval of the State's materials
@ref s 2020(d) (src:1462)
GIVEN `the State determines that the material alters or amends the State plan of operation or conflicts with the rights and levels of benefits to which a household is entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(d) the Secretary may require the State to submit the material for prior approval` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the State determines that the material alters or amends the State plan of operation or conflicts with the rights and levels of benefits to which a household is entitled`
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary may not, as a part of the approval process for a plan of operation, require a State to submit for prior approval"
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the State determines" lifts the bar and grants the Secretary nothing
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2020(d) the Secretary's finding on a reservation` HAS
    `the Secretary determines that the State agency is failing properly to administer the program on the reservation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary determines that the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently conducting the program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- src:1462 | In the case of all or part of an Indian reservation, the State agency as defined in section 2012(s)(1) of this title shall be responsible for conducting such program on such reservation unless the Secretary determines that the State agency (as defined in section 2012(s)(1) of this title) is failing, subsequent to August 31, 1964, properly to administer such program on such reservation in accordance with the purposes of this chapter and further determines that the State agency as defined in section 2012(s)(2) of this title is capable of effectively and efficiently conducting such program, in light of the distance of the reservation from State agency-operated certification and issuance centers, the previous experience of such tribal organization in the operation of programs authorized under the Indian Self-Determination Act (25 U.S.C. 450) [Footnote: 1 See References in Text note below.] and similar Acts of Congress, the tribal organization’s management and fiscal capabilities, and the adequacy of measures taken by the tribal organization to ensure that there shall be no discrimination in the operation of the program on the basis of race, color, sex, or national origin, in which event such State agency shall be responsible for conducting such program and submitting for approval a plan of operation specifying the manner in which such program will be conducted. …
-- jural: a tribal organization | the State agency | power and liability: the program on a reservation moves to the tribal organization on the Secretary's two determinations
@ref s 2020(d) (src:1462)
GIVEN `the finding` IS A `s 2020(d) the Secretary's finding on a reservation`
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
`s 2020(d) the party responsible for conducting the program on the reservation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- "unless the Secretary determines" both things: if either determination is that the condition does not hold, the State agency stays responsible
        IF `the finding`'s `the Secretary determines that the State agency is failing properly to administer the program on the reservation` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST `the State agency`
        IF `the finding`'s `the Secretary determines that the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently conducting the program` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST `the State agency`
        IF `the finding`'s `the Secretary determines that the State agency is failing properly to administer the program on the reservation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            AND `the finding`'s `the Secretary determines that the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently conducting the program` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST `a tribal organization`
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a determination of the Secretary was not supplied
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 2020(d) factors the Secretary weighs` HAS
    `the distance of the reservation from State agency-operated certification and issuance centers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the previous experience of the tribal organization in programs authorized under the Indian Self-Determination Act and similar Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tribal organization's management and fiscal capabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the adequacy of measures to ensure there is no discrimination on the basis of race, color, sex, or national origin` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1462 | further determines that the State agency as defined in section 2012(s)(2) of this title is capable of effectively and efficiently conducting such program, in light of the distance of the reservation from State agency-operated certification and issuance centers, the previous experience of such tribal organization in the operation of programs authorized under the Indian Self-Determination Act (25 U.S.C. 450) [Footnote: 1 See References in Text note below.] and similar Acts of Congress, the tribal organization’s management and fiscal capabilities, and the adequacy of measures taken by the tribal organization to ensure that there shall be no discrimination in the operation of the program on the basis of race, color, sex, or national origin, …
-- jural: the Secretary | the tribal organization | power and liability: the Secretary's determination of capability, made in light of four factors; this is the answer to the keel's field for s 2012(s)(2)
@ref s 2020(d) (src:1462)
GIVEN `the Secretary's determination that the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently conducting the program` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the factors the Secretary weighed` IS A `s 2020(d) factors the Secretary weighs`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(d) the Secretary has determined that the tribal organization is capable of conducting the program` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the Secretary's determination that the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently conducting the program`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): no determination was supplied
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF `the factors the Secretary weighed`'s `the distance of the reservation from State agency-operated certification and issuance centers`
            AND `the factors the Secretary weighed`'s `the previous experience of the tribal organization in programs authorized under the Indian Self-Determination Act and similar Acts`
            AND `the factors the Secretary weighed`'s `the tribal organization's management and fiscal capabilities`
            AND `the factors the Secretary weighed`'s `the adequacy of measures to ensure there is no discrimination on the basis of race, color, sex, or national origin`
        THEN JUST d
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in light of the distance of the reservation ..., the previous experience ..., the tribal organization's management and fiscal capabilities, and the adequacy of measures"
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1462 | The Secretary, upon the request of a tribal organization, shall provide the designees of such organization with appropriate training and technical assistance to enable them to qualify as expeditiously as possible as a State agency pursuant to section 2012(s)(2) of this title. …
-- jural: a tribal organization | the Secretary | claim and duty: training and technical assistance for its designees on request
@ref s 2020(d) (src:1462)
GIVEN `a tribal organization has requested training and technical assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(d) the Secretary must provide the designees with training and technical assistance` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a tribal organization has requested training and technical assistance` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary, upon the request of a tribal organization, shall provide"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:1462 | A State agency, as defined in section 2012(s)(1) of this title, before it submits its plan of operation to the Secretary for the administration of the supplemental nutrition assistance program on all or part of an Indian reservation, shall consult in good faith with the tribal organization about that portion of the State’s plan of operation pertaining to the implementation of the program for members of the tribe, and shall implement the program in a manner that is responsive to the needs of the Indians on the reservation as determined by ongoing consultation with the tribal organization.
-- jural: a tribal organization | the State agency | claim and duty: good-faith consultation before the plan is submitted, and a program responsive to the needs of the Indians on the reservation
@ref s 2020(d) (src:1462)
GIVEN `the plan of operation covers all or part of an Indian reservation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has not yet submitted the plan to the Secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2020(d) the State agency must consult in good faith with the tribal organization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the plan of operation covers all or part of an Indian reservation` AND `the State agency has not yet submitted the plan to the Secretary` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before it submits its plan of operation to the Secretary ... on all or part of an Indian reservation"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
